New interceptor API incorrectly decodes headers as utf-8, not byte strings

## Bug Description

In the old interceptor API, using `onHeaders()` would get raw headers as an array `[headerName1, headerValue1, headerName2, headerValue2, ...]`, where each value was a `Buffer`. This is nice for low-level HTTP interception.

In the new interceptor API, using `onResponseStart()` gets the headers as an object literal, `{ headerName1: headerValue1, headerName2: headerValue2, ... }`, where each value is strings (or probably an array of strings in some cases). This is reasonable.

However, what is buggy is the decoding of these headers. Headers should be turned into strings using [isomorphic decoding](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#isomorphic-decode). The new API appears to instead use UTF-8.

## Reproducible By

```js
// undici NEW handler API decodes headers as UTF-8 instead of isomorphic decode
const net = require("net");
const { getGlobalDispatcher } = require("undici");

const server = net.createServer(socket => {
  socket.once("data", () => {
    // Header with bytes 0xE2 0x80 0xA6 - should be 3 isomorphic-decoded chars, not 1 UTF-8 char
    socket.end(Buffer.concat([
      Buffer.from("HTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\nX-Test: "),
      Buffer.from([0xE2, 0x80, 0xA6]),
      Buffer.from("\r\nContent-Length: 0\r\n\r\n")
    ]));
  });
});

server.listen(0, "127.0.0.1", async () => {
  const opts = { origin: `http://127.0.0.1:${server.address().port}`, path: "/", method: "GET" };

  // OLD API - correct
  await new Promise(r => getGlobalDispatcher().dispatch(opts, {
    onConnect() {},
    onHeaders(status, raw) {
      for (let i = 0; i < raw.length; i += 2)
        if (raw[i].toString().toLowerCase() === "x-test") {
          const v = raw[i + 1].toString("latin1"); // actually isomorphic decode, not latin1 = windows-1252
          console.log("OLD API: length", v.length, "chars", [...v].map(c => c.charCodeAt(0).toString(16)).join(" "));
        }
    },
    onData() {},
    onComplete() { r(); },
    onError(e) { console.log(e); r(); }
  }));

  // NEW API - bug: decodes as UTF-8
  await new Promise(r => getGlobalDispatcher().dispatch(opts, {
    onRequestStart() {},
    onResponseStart(ctrl, status, headers) {
      const v = headers["x-test"];
      console.log("NEW API: length", v.length, "chars", [...v].map(c => c.charCodeAt(0).toString(16)).join(" "));
      r();
    }
  }));

  server.close();
});
```

## Expected Behavior

`NEW API` should give the same results as `OLD API`.

## Environment

- Node.js: v25.3.0
- undici: 7.18.2

### Additional context

This makes it hard for jsdom to pass certain web platform tests when using the new undici interceptors API.

